title: $:/themes/tiddlywiki/opaline/sticky
tags: [[$:/tags/Stylesheet]]
code-body: yes

<!-- When sticky titles are enabled, vanilla gives the title an opaque
     background (tiddler-background). Override it to match THIS theme's panel
     surface so the stuck header stays consistent. Higher specificity than
     vanilla's rule; only emitted while sticky is on.

     This used to be far more involved: the title was made fully transparent
     and the frost was painted on a ::before pseudo-element, because putting
     `backdrop-filter` on the title itself turned it into a backdrop root and
     left the tiddler toolbar's nested dropdown with nothing to sample, so that
     popup rendered clear and unblurred. There was an @supports fallback under
     it for browsers without blur. None of that is needed now that surfaces are
     opaque — the whole class of bug came from the glass.

     The title already carries its own bottom hairline from story.tid, which is
     what keeps body text from scrolling invisibly under the stuck header. -->
<$reveal state="$:/themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/options/stickytitles" type="match" text="yes">
``
.tc-story-river .tc-tiddler-title {
	background: var(--o-paper);
}
``
</$reveal>
